# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator backpropagation {#operator-backpropagation}"
msgstr "Operator backpropagation {#operator-backpropagation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package implements operator backpropagation (OBP) for reducing depth of circuits in expectation value calculations. This technique propagates an observable backward through gates at the end of a quantum circuit, which results in a more shallow circuit at the cost of an increase in observable measurement bases. As one backpropagates an operator further through a circuit, the size of the observable grows exponentially, resulting in both a classical and quantum resource overhead. However, for some circuits, the resulting distribution of Pauli observables is more concentrated than the worst-case exponential scaling, meaning that some terms in the Hamiltonian with small coefficients can be truncated to reduce the quantum overhead. The error incurred by doing this can be controlled to find a suitable tradeoff between precision and efficiency.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapatupad ng package na ito ang operator backpropagation (OBP) para bawasan ang depth ng mga circuit sa mga kalkulasyon ng expectation value. Ipinapasa ng teknik na ito ang isang observable pabalik sa mga gate sa dulo ng isang quantum circuit, na nagreresulta sa mas mababaw na circuit kapalit ng pagdami ng mga measurement basis ng observable. Habang mas malayo ang pag-backpropagate ng operator sa circuit, exponential ang paglaki ng observable, na nagdudulot ng overhead sa parehong classical at quantum na resources. Gayunpaman, para sa ilang circuit, mas nakakonsentra ang resultang distribusyon ng mga Pauli observable kaysa sa worst-case na exponential scaling, ibig sabihin ay may mga term sa Hamiltonian na maliliit ang coefficient na maaaring i-truncate para mabawasan ang quantum overhead. Makokontrol ang error na dulot nito para makahanap ng angkop na balanse sa pagitan ng precision at efficiency.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are a number of ways in which operator backpropagation can be performed, this package uses a method based on Clifford perturbation theory, which has the benefit that the overhead incurred by backpropagating various gates is determined by the non-Cliffordness of that gate. This leads to an increased efficiency for some families of circuits relative to tensor-network based methods for OBP, which currently have high classical overheads even in cases where the quantum overhead remains tame.\n"
msgstr "Maraming paraan para magawa ang operator backpropagation. Gumagamit ang package na ito ng method na batay sa Clifford perturbation theory, na may benepisyong ang overhead na dulot ng pag-backpropagate ng iba't ibang gate ay natutukoy ng non-Cliffordness ng gate na iyon. Nagdudulot ito ng mas mataas na efficiency para sa ilang pamilya ng mga circuit kumpara sa mga tensor-network-based na method para sa OBP, na kasalukuyang may mataas na classical overhead kahit sa mga kasong nananatiling mababa ang quantum overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package is suitable for estimating expectation values of general quantum circuits and Pauli observables; however, for high-magic (very non-Clifford) circuits the observable error incurred from truncation will likely become prohibitive before the observable has been propagated through a meaningful portion of the circuit. For near-Clifford circuits, it may be possible to propagate through much more of the circuit while maintaining relatively small error bounds.\n"
msgstr "Angkop ang package na ito para sa pagtantya ng mga expectation value ng pangkalahatang quantum circuit at Pauli observable; gayunpaman, para sa mga circuit na high-magic (napaka-non-Clifford), malamang na maging hadlang ang observable error mula sa truncation bago pa maipasa ang observable sa makabuluhang bahagi ng circuit. Para sa mga near-Clifford na circuit, maaaring posibleng maipasa ito sa mas malaking bahagi ng circuit habang nananatiling maliit ang mga error bound.\n"

