msgid "Use case examples {#use-case-examples}"
msgstr "Mga halimbawa ng use case {#use-case-examples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This technique has been used to implement lower-depth Trotter circuits for the time-evolution of a 2D spin model [\\[1\\]](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41534-026-01196-0).\n"
msgstr "Ginamit ang teknik na ito para magpatupad ng mga Trotter circuit na mas mababa ang depth para sa time-evolution ng isang 2D spin model [\\[1\\]](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41534-026-01196-0).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Technical discussion {#technical-discussion}"
msgstr "Teknikal na talakayan {#technical-discussion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A single entry point:** the `backpropagate` function performs OBP.\n"
msgstr "**Iisang entry point:** ang function na `backpropagate` ang nagsasagawa ng OBP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two independent controls over the depth ↔ accuracy tradeoff:**\n"
msgstr "**Dalawang independiyenteng kontrol sa tradeoff ng depth ↔ accuracy:**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`OperatorBudget` bounds how large the observable may grow during backpropagation.\n"
msgstr "Nililimitahan ng `OperatorBudget` kung gaano kalaki ang maaaring lumaki ng observable habang nagba-backpropagate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`TruncationErrorBudget` bounds how much error may be incurred during backpropagation.\n"
msgstr "Nililimitahan ng `TruncationErrorBudget` kung gaano karaming error ang maaaring maidulot habang nagba-backpropagate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Effectiveness depends on how Clifford the circuit is:** for high-magic circuits (i.e. very non-Clifford), terms added to the observable tend to have larger coefficients, so one incurs more truncation error earlier, limiting the depth savings under a fixed error budget. Near-Clifford circuits can be truncated more aggressively and backpropagated deeper under the same budget.\n"
msgstr "**Nakasalalay ang bisa sa kung gaano ka-Clifford ang circuit:** para sa mga high-magic na circuit (ibig sabihin, napaka-non-Clifford), ang mga term na idinaragdag sa observable ay may posibilidad na magkaroon ng mas malalaking coefficient, kaya mas maaga ang pagkakaroon ng truncation error, na naglilimita sa matitipid na depth sa ilalim ng nakatakdang error budget. Ang mga near-Clifford na circuit ay maaaring i-truncate nang mas agresibo at ma-backpropagate nang mas malalim sa ilalim ng parehong budget.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Fully introspectable:** each run returns an `OBPMetadata` object recording per-slice Pauli counts, QWC-group counts, and accumulated truncation error, with `plot_*` helpers to visualize operator growth and error against circuit depth — useful for tuning budgets before committing QPU time.\n"
msgstr "**Lubos na masusuri:** bawat run ay nagbabalik ng `OBPMetadata` object na nagtatala ng bilang ng Pauli bawat slice, bilang ng QWC group, at naipong truncation error, kasama ang mga helper na `plot_*` para i-visualize ang paglaki ng operator at ang error laban sa depth ng circuit — kapaki-pakinabang para sa pag-tune ng mga budget bago gumamit ng oras ng QPU.\n"

